{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "a9b8c7d6-e5f4-4321-ba98-76543210fedc",
		"name": "GameVault - Sprint 1 REST API Verification Suite",
		"description": "# GameVault – Sprint 1 REST API Live Demonstration Suite\n\nAutomated Postman test suite for GameVault Sprint 1 (PR1 evaluation). Covers US-10 (View Library), US-09 (Add Game), and US-11 (Remove Game) with automated status code assertions, header verifications, and error handling checks.\n\n### Teacher Live Demo Quick Guide:\n1. Ensure Spring Boot backend is running locally (`./gradlew bootRun` on port 8080) or in Docker (`docker run -p 8080:8080 ...`).\n2. Select the **'GameVault Local Environment'** from the top-right environment selector in Postman (baseUrl: `http://localhost:8080`).\n3. Click **'Run Collection'** to execute all 8 requests automatically (16/16 green tests in <2s).\n4. Walk through individual requests:\n   - **US-10:** `GET /api/library` shows 200 OK and seed data (*Hades*, *Elden Ring*, *Hollow Knight*).\n   - **US-09:** `POST /api/library` shows 201 Created and `Location` header.\n   - **Validation:** POST with blank title or missing status shows 400 Bad Request with structured field errors.\n   - **Not Found:** GET or DELETE on ID `999` shows 404 Not Found.\n   - **US-11:** `DELETE /api/library/:id` shows 204 No Content.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "baseUrl",
			"value": "http://localhost:8080",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "createdGameId",
			"value": "1",
			"type": "string"
		}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "US-10: GET /api/library (Get All Games)",
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"exec": [
							"pm.test(\"Status code is 200 OK\", function () {",
							"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
							"});",
							"",
							"pm.test(\"Response is a valid JSON array\", function () {",
							"    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
							"    pm.expect(Array.isArray(jsonData)).to.be.true;",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.length).to.be.at.least(1);",
							"});",
							"",
							"pm.test(\"Items contain required fields: id, title, status\", function () {",
							"    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
							"    const firstItem = jsonData[0];",
							"    pm.expect(firstItem).to.have.property('id');",
							"    pm.expect(firstItem).to.have.property('title');",
							"    pm.expect(firstItem).to.have.property('status');",
							"});"
						],
						"type": "text/javascript"
					}
				}
			],
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "Accept",
						"value": "application/json"
					}
				],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/library",
					"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
					"path": ["api", "library"]
				},
				"description": "Retrieves the full list of games currently tracked in the personal library."
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "US-10: GET /api/library/:id (Get Single Game by ID)",
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"exec": [
							"pm.test(\"Status code is 200 OK\", function () {",
							"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
							"});",
							"",
							"pm.test(\"Returns correct game details for ID 1 (Hades)\", function () {",
							"    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.id).to.eql(1);",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.title).to.eql(\"Hades\");",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql(\"PLAYING\");",
							"});"
						],
						"type": "text/javascript"
					}
				}
			],
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "Accept",
						"value": "application/json"
					}
				],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/library/1",
					"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
					"path": ["api", "library", "1"]
				},
				"description": "Retrieves specific game details by its numeric ID."
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "US-10: GET /api/library/999 (Non-existent Game -> 404)",
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
